# Giai đoạn 1 checkpoint allows ".trivyignore có lý do" (a documented reason) as the alternative
# to "0 HIGH/CRITICAL". Reasoning below — this is NOT "ignore and forget", it's "known, real,
# tracked, and the actual fix needs more than this stage's scope".
#
# Context: bumping spring-boot-starter-parent 3.2.4 -> 3.2.12 (see pom.xml comment) already cut
# the HIGH/CRITICAL count from 36 to 31 (verified: `trivy image --severity HIGH,CRITICAL
# bss/customer-service:test`, run twice, before/after). 3.2.12 is the LAST patch release of the
# 3.2.x line (checked against Maven Central's maven-metadata.xml) — every remaining CVE below
# needs a Spring Boot 3.3.x or 3.4.x line to get a fix (Tomcat 9.0.121/10.1.58/11.0.25,
# Spring Framework 6.2.x, Jackson 2.18.8+). That's a minor-version framework migration
# (deprecations, possible breaking changes across all 5 backend services + api-gateway,
# re-verifying every *IT test) — real work that deserves its own dedicated pass, not something
# to rush inside an already-large Giai đoạn 1 change. Tracked as a follow-up (open as its own
# issue: "Nâng Spring Boot 3.2.x -> 3.3/3.4 LTS để dọn sạch Trivy findings").
#
# Re-run `trivy image --severity HIGH,CRITICAL bss/customer-service:test` after that migration
# and delete this file once it comes back clean (or shrink this list to whatever's left).

